course: dictionary
lesson: 15133
title: Short words for instruments
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some long words are shortened in everyday talk. Sax is a short, informal word for saxophone. «Mia plays the sax in the school band.» The words play and band are clues that a sax is a musical instrument.
explain: A sax is curved and made of metal, and you play it by blowing into it. The sentence tells you what to do with it: you play it. Try the meaning in the sentence: «Mia plays the saxophone in the school band» still makes sense, so sax means saxophone.
explain: Be careful: the sax is made of brass, which is a metal, but in music lessons it counts as a woodwind instrument. Musicians play it with a reed, a thin strip that vibrates when you blow. A dictionary will confirm any word you are unsure of.
fact: Sax is a short, informal word for saxophone.
fact: A sax is a curved metal wind instrument played with a reed.
fact: The sax is often used in jazz and pop music.
fact: In music lessons the sax is a woodwind instrument, even though it is made of brass.
fact: You can say «play the sax» when you talk about playing this instrument.
exercise: «Mia plays the sax in the school band.» What is a sax? | *A musical instrument | A kind of car | A type of hat | A sports game
exercise: Sax is a short word. What is it short for? | Saxony | Saxon | *Saxophone | Sandwich
exercise: Which kind of music often uses the sax? | Marching songs for soldiers | Ballet | Opera | *Jazz
test: Sax is an informal word. Which word means the same thing but is longer? | Sack | *Saxophone | Saxon | Saxe
test: In music lessons, which family of instruments is the sax in? | *Woodwind | Percussion | String | Keyboard
exam: «The jazz band's sax player blew a long, smooth note.» What is a sax player? | *Someone who plays the sax | Someone who fixes cars | Someone who paints pictures | Someone who sells tickets
